---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Student portal"
  path="/docs/user-guide/student-portal"
  description="What students can do in the KoAkademy student portal — classes, schedule, tuition, digital ID, and notifications."
>
  <p>
    The Student Portal is the React-based workspace for enrolled students. Your
    school controls which areas are enabled, so some features described here may
    not appear on your account.
  </p>

  <h2>Dashboard</h2>
  <p>
    After signing in, the dashboard shows your current enrollment status, upcoming
    classes, announcements, and shortcuts to the areas you use most. First-time
    users see a short onboarding checklist that can be dismissed once completed.
  </p>

  <h2>Classes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Open a class to see <strong>posts and materials</strong> from your teacher.</li>
    <li>Submit <strong>assignment submissions</strong> directly from the class page before the deadline.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Schedule</h2>
  <p>
    The schedule page shows your weekly class timetable for the active semester.
    Printable timetable PDFs can be downloaded when your school enables them.
  </p>

  <h2>Tuition and statements of account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The <strong>tuition</strong> area shows your current assessment and payment
      status.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Statements of account (SOA)</strong> issued by the cashier appear
      here with download links. Each SOA carries a signed verification link so
      third parties (such as sponsors or employers) can confirm it is genuine.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Digital ID card</h2>
  <p>
    Your <strong>digital ID card</strong> shows your student photo, identifier,
    and a QR code. Staff and verification kiosks can scan the code to confirm
    your enrollment status through the public verification page — no account
    needed for verification.
  </p>

  <h2>Announcements and notifications</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Announcements</strong> from the school appear on your dashboard and
      in the announcements page.
    </li>
    <li>
      The <strong>Notification Center</strong> collects messages sent to you —
      enrollment updates, grade releases, payment notices, class suspensions,
      school events, and reminders.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Help and support</h2>
  <p>
    If something is wrong with a record or you cannot access a feature, open a
    <strong>help ticket</strong> from the portal instead of sharing your account.
    Staff responses appear in the same thread.
  </p>

  <h2>Profile and security</h2>
  <p>
    From profile settings you can update your information (where permitted),
    enable <strong>two-factor authentication</strong>, register
    <strong>passkeys</strong>, and manage personal <strong>API keys</strong> when
    your school allows them.
  </p>
  <div class="doc-callout doc-callout-tip">
    <p class="doc-callout-label">Keep your account private</p>
    <p>
      School staff will never ask for your password. Use two-factor
      authentication and report suspicious sign-in prompts through a help
      ticket.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
